{
  "$comment": [
    "H3, the usage batch: POST /v1/usage, a factory's usage rows per (factory, session_id, day), from its",
    "organizer to its own record and from that record's forwarder to Hestia. Spec: hestia",
    "docs/specs/usage-rows.md (Contract, Amendment 1 FR-6, Amendment 2). Map: agent-slack",
    "docs/contracts/factory-contract-map.md H3. Sample rule and index: contracts/README.md.",
    "How a case is posted: {\"factory\": <the key's factory>, \"rows\": [<row>]} for a valid case; for a",
    "must_refuse case, rows is [valid[0].row, <row>], so a refused row sits at index 1 beside a valid one;",
    "a case with `count` instead of `row` is that many copies of valid[`copies`].row, each with its",
    "session_id suffixed -<n>. `where` is `batch` (the whole body refused, nothing stored) or `row` (the row",
    "is answered in `rejected` and every other row is stored). `reason_contains` is a substring of the",
    "batch error or of the rejected row's `reason`. `stored` is what the reader keeps of a valid row; every",
    "valid case's day is in `week`, which is what GET /v1/usage?week= sums of them all."
  ],
  "contract": "H3",
  "endpoint": "POST /v1/usage",
  "writers": [
    {"repo": "agent-organizer (Deltagos)", "code": "internal/service/usagepost.go", "test": "internal/service/usagepost_test.go"},
    {"repo": "record (the forwarder, a row it already accepted)", "code": "internal/forward/usage.go", "test": "internal/forward/usage_integration_test.go"}
  ],
  "readers": [
    {"repo": "record", "code": "internal/usage",
     "tests": ["internal/usage/usage_test.go", "internal/usage/migration_integration_test.go", "internal/handler/usage_integration_test.go"]}
  ],
  "limits": {"max_rows": 500, "max_body_bytes": 33554432},
  "batch_keys": ["factory", "rows"],
